<title>FRANCE: New French premier's first outing set for Sweden.</title>
<headline>New French premier's first outing set for Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's new Socialist Prime Minister Lionel Jospin is to make his first official trip abroad on Thursday, going to Malmoe, Sweden, for a meeting of Socialist heads of government and parties, aides said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Jospin is to address the meeting on Friday and also hold talks with Britain's new Labour Prime Minister Tony Blair, who swept to power just one month ago.</p>
</text>
